      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy teeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like a flock ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of sheep that are even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shorn, which came up from the washing; all of which bear twins, and none ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " barren among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy lips ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like a thread of scarlet, and thy speech ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " comely: thy temples ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like a piece of pomegranate within thy locks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy neck ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like the tower of David built for an armory, on which hang a thousand bucklers, all shields of mighty men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy two breasts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like two young roes that are twins, which feed among the lilies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Until the day shall break, and the shadows flee away, I will repair to the mountain of myrrh, and to the hill of frankincense.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all fair, my love; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no spot in thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come with me from Lebanon, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " spouse, with me from Lebanon: look from the top of Amana, from the top of Shenir and Hermon, from the lions' dens, from the mountains of the leopards.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast ravished my heart, my sister, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " spouse; thou hast ravished my heart with one of thy eyes, with one chain of thy neck.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How fair is thy love, my sister, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " spouse! how much better is thy love than wine! and the smell of thy ointments than all spices!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy lips, O ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " spouse, drop ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the honey-comb; honey and milk ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under thy tongue; and the smell of thy garments ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like the smell of Lebanon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A garden inclosed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my sister, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " spouse; a spring shut up, a fountain sealed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy plants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an orchard of pomegranates, with pleasant fruits; camphor, with spikenard,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:SNG.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Spikenard and saffron; calamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
